<title>SOUTH KOREA: SKorean BOK sells dollars at 870.00 to support won.</title>
<headline>SKorean BOK sells dollars at 870.00 to support won.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The central Bank of Korea sold dollars during Friday's early morning trading to slow the local currency's fall, dealers said.</p>
<p>They said the bank stepped in when the won fell to the 870 level.</p>
<p>The central bank has refused to confirm or deny that it intervenes in the market.</p>
<p>The won rose to 869.40 just after the intervention.</p>
<p>Dealers said the dollar's bullish trend would be difficult to stem due to the widening trade deficit and the U.S. unit's strength on world markets.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
